{"id":"2e4ee9615831113b","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-expectation.md","title":"Expectation","display":"df-expectation — Expectation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-expectation","aliases":["58-df-expectation","Expectation"],"display":"df-expectation — Expectation","depends_on":["[[58-df-probability-space]]","[[58-df-integral]]","[[58-df-sigma-algebra]]","[[58-df-L1]]","[[58-df-measurable-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-expectation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-expectation</span><span>Expectation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-expectation — Expectation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space\">58-df-probability-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"58-df-integral\">58-df-integral</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"58-df-sigma-algebra\">58-df-sigma-algebra</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ec5f34b0092e1daf\" href=\"?note=ec5f34b0092e1daf\" title=\"58-df-L1\">58-df-L1</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"58-df-measurable-function\">58-df-measurable-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,Y,f\\in V\">\\(X,Y,f\\in V\\)</span> (complex-valued random variables represented by measurable functions)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{P}\">\\(\\mathbb{P}\\)</span> (probability measure)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\">\\(\\Omega\\)</span> (sample space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (ambient <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-algebra) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal G\\subseteq\\Sigma\">\\(\\mathcal G\\subseteq\\Sigma\\)</span> (conditioning <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-algebra)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,f,E;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,f,E;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (integral-value predicate defined here from nonnegative integrals)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ExpectedValue}_S(z,X;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\operatorname{ExpectedValue}_S(z,X;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (expectation-value predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> (integrable-representative and measurable-function predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{CondExp}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{CondExp}_S\\)</span> (fully parameterized conditional-expectation predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{CondExp}\">\\(\\operatorname{CondExp}\\)</span> (three-place compatibility predicate)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}integrable\\text{-}complex\\text{-}integral} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,f,E;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(f;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land E\\in\\Sigma\\land\nz=\n\\int_E\\max(\\operatorname{Re}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P-\n\\int_E\\max(-\\operatorname{Re}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P\n+i\\left(\n\\int_E\\max(\\operatorname{Im}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P-\n\\int_E\\max(-\\operatorname{Im}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P\n\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}integrable\\text{-}complex\\text{-}integral} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,f,E;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(f;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land E\\in\\Sigma\\land\nz=\n\\int_E\\max(\\operatorname{Re}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P-\n\\int_E\\max(-\\operatorname{Re}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P\n+i\\left(\n\\int_E\\max(\\operatorname{Im}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P-\n\\int_E\\max(-\\operatorname{Im}\\circ f,0)\\,d\\mathbb P\n\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}expectation} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{ExpectedValue}_S(z,X;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\Sigma)\\land\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,X,\\Omega;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}expectation} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{ExpectedValue}_S(z,X;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\Sigma)\\land\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,X,\\Omega;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conditional\\text{-}expectation} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,X,\\mathcal G,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\Sigma)\\land\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal G,\\Omega)\\land\\mathcal G\\subseteq\\Sigma\\land\n\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(X;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land\n\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(Y;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(Y;(\\Omega,\\mathcal G),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)))\\land\n\\forall A\\in\\mathcal G\\;\\exists z\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,Y,A;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,X,A;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conditional\\text{-}expectation} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,X,\\mathcal G,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S(\\mathbb P,\\Omega,\\Sigma)\\land\n\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal G,\\Omega)\\land\\mathcal G\\subseteq\\Sigma\\land\n\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(X;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land\n\\mathrm{IntegrableFunction}_S(Y;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(Y;(\\Omega,\\mathcal G),(\\mathbb C,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb C)))\\land\n\\forall A\\in\\mathcal G\\;\\exists z\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,Y,A;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\land\n\\operatorname{ComplexIntegral}_S(z,X,A;\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conditional\\text{-}expectation\\text{-}compatibility} \\vdash \\operatorname{CondExp}(Y,X,\\mathcal G)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P\\;\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,X,\\mathcal G,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}conditional\\text{-}expectation\\text{-}compatibility} \\vdash \\operatorname{CondExp}(Y,X,\\mathcal G)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P\\;\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,X,\\mathcal G,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb P)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Expectation is an explicitly typed integral value, not an application of the upstream nonnegative-integral notation to an arbitrary signed or complex function.</li>\n<li>The complex integral is constructed from the four nonnegative parts of the real and imaginary components.</li>\n<li>Conditional expectation includes the ambient probability space, integrability, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal G\">\\(\\mathcal G\\)</span>-measurability, and equality of integrals on every event in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal G\">\\(\\mathcal G\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^p\">\\(L^p\\)</span> spaces: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{E}[|X|^p]^{1/p}\">\\(\\mathbb{E}[|X|^p]^{1/p}\\)</span> defines <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^p\">\\(L^p\\)</span>-norm</li>\n<li>Tower rule: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[X \\mid \\mathcal{F}_1] \\mid \\mathcal{F}_2] = \\mathbb{E}[X \\mid \\mathcal{F}_2]\">\\(\\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[X \\mid \\mathcal{F}_1] \\mid \\mathcal{F}_2] = \\mathbb{E}[X \\mid \\mathcal{F}_2]\\)</span></li>\n<li>Law of total expectation: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{E}[X] = \\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[X \\mid Y]]\">\\(\\mathbb{E}[X] = \\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[X \\mid Y]]\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Williams, Probability with Martingales</li>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-probability-space","status":"resolved","id":"05